WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.925
What breaks in production,
and what guards against it?

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:07.296
A live run on the wrong cloud or tenant
reports another estate as this one,

3
00:00:07.296 --> 00:00:11.156
so the kit checks the CLI's cloud
and tenant before its first call,

4
00:00:11.156 --> 00:00:12.613
and has no default cloud.

5
00:00:12.613 --> 00:00:16.489
A query without a scope covers
whatever the account happens to see,

6
00:00:16.489 --> 00:00:20.013
so every query takes the management
group from the settings.

7
00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:23.313
A response's next link
could point at another host,

8
00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:27.499
so any URL off the commercial
Resource Manager host is refused.

9
00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:32.077
An unverified call could misread
a property and report a false gap,

10
00:00:32.077 --> 00:00:36.488
so it's refused in a live run unless
you allow it, and Lab 2 compares.

11
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:40.080
And the run folder never
goes in a public repository.
